# Spring Boot CRUD API

A Spring Boot REST API demonstrating CRUD operations for employees using Spring Data JPA, `JpaRepository`, and Spring Security with JDBC authentication.

## Overview

This project is part of my Spring Boot learning journey.

The project initially used a custom DAO implementation with JPA `EntityManager` to perform database operations. It was later refactored to use Spring Data JPA and `JpaRepository`, reducing the amount of boilerplate code required for database access.

The API supports full CRUD operations as well as partial updates using HTTP PATCH.

The project was then extended with Spring Security to implement authentication and role-based authorization. Authentication was initially implemented using in-memory users and was later refactored to use JDBC-based authentication with a MySQL database.

## Project Evolution

### Version 1 - Custom DAO

The project initially used a custom DAO layer with JPA `EntityManager`.

    REST Controller
          ↓
    Service Layer
          ↓
    DAO Interface
          ↓
    DAO Implementation
          ↓
    JPA EntityManager
          ↓
    MySQL Database

### Version 2 - Spring Data JPA

The custom DAO interface and implementation were replaced with a Spring Data JPA repository.

    REST Controller
          ↓
    Service Layer
          ↓
    EmployeeRepository
          ↓
    JpaRepository
          ↓
    MySQL Database

This refactoring simplified the data access layer by using the built-in CRUD operations provided by `JpaRepository`.

### Version 3 - Spring Security

Spring Security was added to protect the REST API using HTTP Basic Authentication and role-based authorization.

The project initially used in-memory users for authentication and was later changed to JDBC authentication.

    HTTP Request
          ↓
    Spring Security
          ↓
    JDBC Authentication
          ↓
    MySQL Database
          ↓
    users / authorities

Different roles have different permissions for the employee endpoints.

