## REST Endpoints

### Get All Employees

    GET /api/employees

Requires the `EMPLOYEE` role.

Returns a list of all employees.

### Get Employee by ID

    GET /api/employees/{employeeId}

Requires the `EMPLOYEE` role.

Returns an employee using the provided ID.

Example:

    GET /api/employees/1

### Create Employee

    POST /api/employees

Requires the `MANAGER` role.

Example request body:

    {
        "firstName": "Ahmed",
        "lastName": "Sabra",
        "email": "ahmed@example.com"
    }

### Update Employee

    PUT /api/employees

Requires the `MANAGER` role.

Example request body:

    {
        "id": 1,
        "firstName": "Ahmed",
        "lastName": "Sabra",
        "email": "new@email.com"
    }

### Delete Employee

    DELETE /api/employees/{employeeId}

Requires the `ADMIN` role.

Example:

    DELETE /api/employees/1

### Partial Update

    PATCH /api/employees/{employeeId}

Requires the `MANAGER` role.

Allows updating specific fields without sending the complete Employee object.

Example:

    {
        "email": "updated@email.com"
    }

## Security

The application uses Spring Security to protect the REST API.

### Authentication

The application uses HTTP Basic Authentication.

User authentication is handled using JDBC and stored in the MySQL database.

Spring Security retrieves users and their authorities through `JdbcUserDetailsManager`.

### Authorization

Access to endpoints is controlled using roles.

| HTTP Method | Endpoint | Required Role |
|-------------|----------|---------------|
| GET | `/api/employees` | EMPLOYEE |
| GET | `/api/employees/{employeeId}` | EMPLOYEE |
| POST | `/api/employees` | MANAGER |
| PUT | `/api/employees` | MANAGER |
| PATCH | `/api/employees/{employeeId}` | MANAGER |
| DELETE | `/api/employees/{employeeId}` | ADMIN |

The application uses `hasRole()` to restrict access based on the authenticated user's role.

