## What I Learned

Through this project, I practiced:

- Building REST APIs with Spring Boot
- Understanding HTTP methods such as GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, and DELETE
- Using `@RestController`
- Using `@RequestMapping`
- Using `@GetMapping`, `@PostMapping`, `@PutMapping`, `@PatchMapping`, and `@DeleteMapping`
- Using `@PathVariable`
- Using `@RequestBody`
- Converting JSON requests into Java objects
- Returning Java objects as JSON responses
- Creating POJO/Entity classes
- Using JPA `EntityManager`
- Creating a custom DAO layer
- Applying the Service Layer pattern
- Using Spring Data JPA
- Extending `JpaRepository`
- Using built-in repository methods such as `findAll()`, `findById()`, `save()`, and `deleteById()`
- Refactoring a custom DAO implementation to Spring Data JPA
- Implementing CRUD database operations
- Implementing partial updates using Jackson `JsonMapper`
- Configuring Spring Security
- Implementing HTTP Basic Authentication
- Implementing JDBC-based authentication
- Understanding users and authorities in Spring Security
- Implementing role-based authorization
- Configuring endpoint access based on HTTP methods and roles
- Understanding the difference between authentication and authorization
- Configuring CSRF for a REST API

